WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.940
For over a decade,

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.960
Bernie Calderon Magtalas has helped the
Philippine Government decide which

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.220
energy, transport, and climate
investments are worth making.

00:00:09.835 --> 00:00:12.795
He started at the Department
of Energy in 2015,

00:00:12.795 --> 00:00:15.595
and is now a Supervising
Economic Development Specialist

00:00:15.595 --> 00:00:18.395
at the Department of Economy,
Planning, and Development.

00:00:19.009 --> 00:00:21.069
Thirty-four infrastructure projects.

00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:24.039
USD 14.05 billion.

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:27.869
Airports, roads, rail, energy, and ports.

00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:31.382
All appraised under the ICC
review framework,

00:00:31.382 --> 00:00:33.842
covering financial and economic models;

00:00:33.842 --> 00:00:39.002
market, technical, social, environmental,
institutional, and gender analyses;

00:00:39.002 --> 00:00:42.063
including concessions, risk,
and prequalification for

00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:44.142
Public-Private Partnership
projects.

00:00:44.751 --> 00:00:47.181
Fifteen development partner programs.

00:00:47.181 --> 00:00:48.941
Twelve consulting studies.

00:00:48.941 --> 00:00:51.791
Forty-eight bills, laws, and policies.

00:00:51.791 --> 00:00:54.391
And eight national boards
and committees advised.

00:00:55.148 --> 00:00:58.938
He built the Philippines' first Regional
Infrastructure Development Index,

00:00:58.938 --> 00:01:05.098
and a model ranking 207 projects in a
USD 176 billion investment pipeline.

00:01:05.706 --> 00:01:08.786
A JICA scholar and Waseda
University graduate,

00:01:08.786 --> 00:01:12.446
he was a Congress Future Energy
Leader of the World Energy Council,

00:01:12.446 --> 00:01:17.066
and is part of the OECD Regional Knowledge
Network on Sustainable Infrastructure,

00:01:17.066 --> 00:01:20.546
along with policymakers and
experts across Southeast Asia.

00:01:21.311 --> 00:01:24.401
Click the link for the full
portfolio and accomplishment report.
